                                                        "code": "// br.delay.digital.1.1 -- stereo clean digital delay\n// Created by Brian Riordan, guaguanco127@gmail.com -- https://github.com/guaguanco127/\n// MUST MATCH: the core, the UI by reference and the M4L device embed this same code\n// in1/in2 audio L/R\n// in3 mode 0 Linked, 1 Stereo, 2 Ping-Pong\n// in4 time L ms 1..10000 and in5 time R ms 1..10000\n// in6 xfade ms 5..5000: how long a time change takes to crossfade to the new time\n// in7 feedback 0..1: at 1 the repeats never fade\n// in8 feedback route 0 Straight: each side feeds itself, 1 Cross: each side feeds the other\n// in9 hold 0/1: stop taking input and keep what is on the loop playing forever\n// in10 low cut Hz 20..2000 and in11 high cut Hz 200..20000: tone of the repeats\n// in12 dry/wet % 0..100\n// in13 on/off 1 on, 0 off: off = the dry signal at full level, no echoes\n// out1/out2 audio L/R\n//\n// Why it sounds clean: a time change never moves a read head while it is playing, so the pitch\n// never bends. Each delay line has two read heads. When the time changes, the silent head jumps to the\n// new time and the sound crossfades over to it. If the time is still moving when a crossfade ends,\n// the next one starts from there, so dragging a dial steps cleanly instead of bending.\n// Changes that arrive during a fade are not lost: the latest one is taken when the fade ends.\n// Long fades play both times at once, so the rhythm blurs from one to the other.\n// The two fade gains always add up to 1, not equal power: the crossfade sits inside the feedback\n// loop, and equal power would add up to +3 dB on every pass when both heads play the same sound.\n// The tone filters sit at the playback head: every echo you hear goes through them, and the loop\n// is fed from the filtered signal, so each repeat is a little darker and thinner than the one before.\n// No saturation. Feedback stops at 1, where the repeats hold their level. A safety ceiling on the\n// loop does nothing below 0 dBFS and only stops a full loop that keeps taking input from building up.\n//\n// Each side has two delay lines. The FIRST line holds the input and is read at the side's own time:\n// that is the first echo. The LOOP line holds the feedback and is read at the loop time: those\n// are all the later echoes. The modes only change where the heads go:\n//   Linked     both sides use Time L; loop time = the same, so echoes at t, 2t, 3t\n//   Stereo     each side uses its own time, loop time = its own time\n//   Ping-Pong  each side's first echo at its own time, then both repeat every T = the longer time,\n//              so L 250 / R 500 gives L 250, R 500, L 750, R 1000: alternating every 250 ms\n// Feedback Cross sends each side's repeats to the other side's loop line. Stereo + Cross is the classic\n// ping-pong: each bounce takes the time of the side it lands on. Linked + Cross swaps a stereo image\n// on every repeat. Cross fades over 20 ms: repeats already on the line keep playing, only where\n// they go next fades across.\n// Nothing is switched in or out: a mode change moves heads through the same crossfade as a\n// time change, so the sound never jumps and the tails carry on through the change.\n//\n// HOLD fades the input out and feedback up to 1 over 20 ms, and the loop stops passing through\n// the tone filters, so what is on the loop repeats unchanged forever. Echoes already on their way\n// still land on the loop. Turn Hold off and the loop decays at the Feedback setting again.\n//\n// ON/OFF fades over 20 ms. Off: the echoes fade out and the dry signal comes up to full level,\n// whatever the Dry/Wet. The delay keeps running underneath, so turning it back on never plays\n// old echoes from before it was turned off.\n\n// 10.1 s at 192 kHz: 10000 ms at any sample rate\nDelay firstL(1939200);\nDelay firstR(1939200);\nDelay loopL(1939200);\nDelay loopR(1939200);\nHistory started(0);\nHistory fLcur(0);\nHistory fLnxt(0);\nHistory fLr(0);\nHistory fRcur(0);\nHistory fRnxt(0);\nHistory fRr(0);\nHistory lLcur(0);\nHistory lLnxt(0);\nHistory lLr(0);\nHistory lRcur(0);\nHistory lRnxt(0);\nHistory lRr(0);\nHistory fbS(0);\nHistory holdS(0);\nHistory lowS(80);\nHistory highS(8000);\nHistory mixS(50);\nHistory crossS(0);\nHistory onS(1);\nHistory lowL(0);\nHistory lowR(0);\nHistory highL(0);\nHistory highR(0);\n\n// read all state first\nst = started;\na0 = fLcur;\na1 = fLnxt;\nar = fLr;\nb0 = fRcur;\nb1 = fRnxt;\nbr = fRr;\np0 = lLcur;\np1 = lLnxt;\npr = lLr;\nq0 = lRcur;\nq1 = lRnxt;\nqr = lRr;\nfb = fbS;\nhd = holdS;\nlo = lowS;\nhi = highS;\nmx = mixS;\ncr = crossS;\nen = onS;\nlzL = lowL;\nlzR = lowR;\nhzL = highL;\nhzR = highR;\n\n// controls glide over 20 ms so nothing clicks; the times crossfade instead\nk = 1 - exp(-1 / mstosamps(20));\nfb = fb + (clip(in7, 0, 1) - fb) * k;\ncr = cr + (clip(floor(in8 + 0.5), 0, 1) - cr) * k;\nhd = hd + (clip(floor(in9 + 0.5), 0, 1) - hd) * k;\nlo = lo + (clip(in10, 20, 2000) - lo) * k;\nhi = hi + (clip(in11, 200, 20000) - hi) * k;\nmx = mx + (clip(in12, 0, 100) - mx) * k;\nen = en + (clip(floor(in13 + 0.5), 0, 1) - en) * k;\n\n// HEAD TARGETS for the mode\nmode = clip(floor(in3 + 0.5), 0, 2);\ntL = clip(mstosamps(clip(in4, 1, 10000)), 2, 1939000);\ntR = clip(mstosamps(clip(in5, 1, 10000)), 2, 1939000);\nfirstTL = tL;\nfirstTR = (mode == 0) ? tL : tR;\nloopTL = firstTL;\nloopTR = firstTR;\nif (mode == 2) {\n    loopTL = max(tL, tR);\n    loopTR = loopTL;\n}\n\n// At load every head starts on its target, no crossfade\nif (st == 0) {\n    a0 = firstTL;\n    b0 = firstTR;\n    p0 = loopTL;\n    q0 = loopTR;\n    st = 1;\n}\n\n// CROSSFADES: each line has a playing head, cur, and a spare head, nxt. r is the fade, 0 = idle.\n// Idle and the target has moved: the spare head jumps to the target and the fade starts.\n// Fading: r climbs to 1, then the spare head becomes the playing head and the fade goes idle.\n// The target is only read when a fade starts, so a moving dial gives a chain of clean fades.\ninc = 1 / mstosamps(clip(in6, 5, 5000));\nif (ar == 0) {\n    if (abs(firstTL - a0) > 0.5) {\n        a1 = firstTL;\n        ar = inc;\n    }\n} else {\n    ar = ar + inc;\n    if (ar >= 1) {\n        a0 = a1;\n        ar = 0;\n    }\n}\nif (br == 0) {\n    if (abs(firstTR - b0) > 0.5) {\n        b1 = firstTR;\n        br = inc;\n    }\n} else {\n    br = br + inc;\n    if (br >= 1) {\n        b0 = b1;\n        br = 0;\n    }\n}\nif (pr == 0) {\n    if (abs(loopTL - p0) > 0.5) {\n        p1 = loopTL;\n        pr = inc;\n    }\n} else {\n    pr = pr + inc;\n    if (pr >= 1) {\n        p0 = p1;\n        pr = 0;\n    }\n}\nif (qr == 0) {\n    if (abs(loopTR - q0) > 0.5) {\n        q1 = loopTR;\n        qr = inc;\n    }\n} else {\n    qr = qr + inc;\n    if (qr >= 1) {\n        q0 = q1;\n        qr = 0;\n    }\n}\n\n// read every head before writing. Raised-cosine fade, the two gains add up to 1.\n// An idle line reads one head only\ng = 0;\nfl = firstL.read(a0, interp=\"spline\");\nif (ar > 0) {\n    g = 0.5 - 0.5 * cos(pi * ar);\n    fl = fl * (1 - g) + firstL.read(a1, interp=\"spline\") * g;\n}\nfr = firstR.read(b0, interp=\"spline\");\nif (br > 0) {\n    g = 0.5 - 0.5 * cos(pi * br);\n    fr = fr * (1 - g) + firstR.read(b1, interp=\"spline\") * g;\n}\nll = loopL.read(p0, interp=\"spline\");\nif (pr > 0) {\n    g = 0.5 - 0.5 * cos(pi * pr);\n    ll = ll * (1 - g) + loopL.read(p1, interp=\"spline\") * g;\n}\nlr = loopR.read(q0, interp=\"spline\");\nif (qr > 0) {\n    g = 0.5 - 0.5 * cos(pi * qr);\n    lr = lr * (1 - g) + loopR.read(q1, interp=\"spline\") * g;\n}\ntapL = fl + ll;\ntapR = fr + lr;\n\n// TONE at the playback head: one-pole low cut, the signal minus its own lowpass, then one-pole high cut.\n// Both the output and the loop take the filtered signal, so the tone works even with Feedback at 0\naLo = 1 - exp(-twopi * lo / samplerate);\naHi = 1 - exp(-twopi * min(hi, samplerate * 0.45) / samplerate);\nlzL = lzL + aLo * (tapL - lzL);\nlzR = lzR + aLo * (tapR - lzR);\nhzL = hzL + aHi * ((tapL - lzL) - hzL);\nhzR = hzR + aHi * ((tapR - lzR) - hzR);\n\n// The input goes onto the first lines; Hold fades it out\nfirstL.write(in1 * (1 - hd));\nfirstR.write(in2 * (1 - hd));\n\n// The loop: Straight feeds each side its own repeats, Cross feeds the other side's.\n// Hold raises feedback to 1 and feeds the loop from the unfiltered heads, so it repeats unchanged.\n// SAFETY CEILING: untouched up to 1, which is 0 dBFS; above that a soft knee that never passes 2, which is +6 dBFS\nfbH = fb + (1 - fb) * hd;\nsL = mix(hzL, tapL, hd);\nsR = mix(hzR, tapR, hd);\nwL = fbH * mix(sL, sR, cr);\nwR = fbH * mix(sR, sL, cr);\nwL = (abs(wL) > 1) ? sign(wL) * (1 + tanh(abs(wL) - 1)) : wL;\nwR = (abs(wR) > 1) ? sign(wR) * (1 + tanh(abs(wR) - 1)) : wR;\nloopL.write(wL);\nloopR.write(wR);\n\n// write state last\nstarted = st;\nfLcur = a0;\nfLnxt = a1;\nfLr = ar;\nfRcur = b0;\nfRnxt = b1;\nfRr = br;\nlLcur = p0;\nlLnxt = p1;\nlLr = pr;\nlRcur = q0;\nlRnxt = q1;\nlRr = qr;\nfbS = fb;\nholdS = hd;\nlowS = lo;\nhighS = hi;\nmixS = mx;\ncrossS = cr;\nonS = en;\nlowL = lzL;\nlowR = lzR;\nhighL = hzL;\nhighR = hzR;\n\n// DRY/WET: equal power, so the level stays even across the range. Off: dry at full level, no wet\nang = mx * 0.01 * pi * 0.5;\ndry = mix(1, cos(ang), en);\nwet = sin(ang) * en;\nout1 = in1 * dry + hzL * wet;\nout2 = in2 * dry + hzR * wet;\n"
                                                    }
                                                },
